# Lab server policy (Listing 2).
#
# Networks used by this policy:
#   10.60.0.0/16  lab client machines
#   10.20.0.0/16  lab device network (SMB must never enter)
#
# Inbound is default-deny.  New SSH connections are rate-limited per source
# (5/minute, burst 5) before the general SSH accept rule.  Outbound traffic
# is allowed so the server can initiate connections; their replies arrive as
# ESTABLISHED on INPUT.
*filter
:INPUT DROP [0:0]
:FORWARD DROP [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]

-A INPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -s 10.60.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 22 -m hashlimit --hashlimit-name lab-ssh --hashlimit-above 5/minute --hashlimit-burst 5 --hashlimit-mode srcip -j DROP
-A INPUT -s 10.60.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 22 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -s 10.60.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 80 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -s 10.60.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 443 -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -s 10.60.0.0/16 -p udp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT
# SMB toward lab devices is always blocked; retries remain NEW and are also
# dropped because only accepted packets create connection state.
-A INPUT -d 10.20.0.0/16 -p tcp --dport 445 -j DROP

COMMIT
